flint build: compile to a native executable

Usage:
  flint build [options] [file.fl]

  The executable is named after the file (hello.fl makes ./hello); a package's is
  out/<name>. -o writes it somewhere else.

Options:
  -O0, -O2             no optimization, with debugging aids (default); or optimized
  --overflow=<mode>    integer overflow: trap (default) or wrap
  -o, --output <path>  where to write the executable
  --color=<when>       colored output: auto (default), always or never
  -h, --help           show this help

  Bounds, null, cast and division checks are always on: only 'unsafe' removes them.

Examples:
  flint build hello.fl
  flint build -O2 hello.fl -o bin/hello
  flint build -O2 --overflow=wrap   (in a package)
